- source_job_id: "7080211"
  title: "Senior Staff/Staff Machine Learning Engineer"
  description: "Senior Staff/Staff Machine Learning Engineer-LLM\n\nCompany Introduction\n\
    \nWe exist to wow our customers. We know we’re doing the right thing when we hear\
    \ our customers say, “How did we ever live without Coupang?” Born out of an obsession\
    \ to make shopping, eating, and living easier than ever, we are collectively disrupting\
    \ the multi-billion-dollar commerce industry from the ground up and establishing\
    \ an unparalleled reputation for being leading and reliable force in South Korean\
    \ commerce.\n\nWe are proud to have the best of both worlds — a startup culture\
    \ with the resources of a large global public company. This fuels us to continue\
    \ our growth and launch new services at the sped we have been at since our inception.\
    \ We are all entrepreneurial surrounded by opportunities to drive new initiatives\
    \ and innovations. At our core, we are bold and ambitious people that like to\
    \ get our hands dirty and make a hands-on impact. At Coupang, you will see yourself,\
    \ your colleagues, your team, and the company grow every day.\n\nOur mission to\
    \ build the future of commerce is real. We push the boundaries of what’s possible\
    \ to solve problems and break traditional tradeoffs. Join Coupang now to create\
    \ an epic experience in this always-on, high-tech, and hyper-connected world.\n\
    \nSummary:\n\nAt Coupang, we invest in providing the best product experience for\
    \ our customers. The AI and Knowledge Engineering team’s mission is to provide\
    \ the best possible technical solution to achieve the optimal experience for our\
    \ customers. We innovate and advance the space of Knowledge Graphs, agents, LLMs,\
    \ AI, ML, NLP, and multi-modal models. We are looking for engineers who want to\
    \ work on cutting edge technology, that is the intersection of Semantic knowledge\
    \ bases, agents, NLP, LLM, ML and software engineering. Come join us to help create\
    \ a world class team advancing the AI/NLP/ML/LLM/RL/Knowledge Graph technologies.\n\
    \nThe Role/Responsibilities:\n\nWork on GenAI, self-learning systems to solve\
    \ complex eCommerce scenarios.\n\nDevelop statistical models for predictive and\
    \ compound AI Models\n\nTrain foundational models that can help with building\
    \ learning systems.\n\nDefine process and experiments for an E2E foundation model.\n\
    \nBuild E2E AI pipelines for storing/servicing foundational models.\n\nMentor\
    \ and guide team members on frameworks, methodologies related to data lakes, data\
    \ normalization, dimension reduction, visualization, statistical models.\n\nEnsure\
    \ Model training is security, compliance aware.\n\nCollaborate with cross-team\
    \ members to understand the requirements ensuring the foundational models, knowledge\
    \ captured aligns with the company’s overall AI strategy.\n\nWhat you will bring/\
    \ Requirements:\n\nOverall 10+ years of working in software engineering and AI/ML\
    \ Engineering.\n\n4+ years of demonstrated data science, experience in building\
    \ large scale foundational models for eCommerce scenarios.\n\nExpertise in large\
    \ language model fine-tuning and deployment.\n\nDeep understanding of AI/ML/Deep-learning\
    \ and statistical model architecture.\n\nStrong statistical/mathematical background\
    \ in defining metrics, learning functions and result analysis.\n\nSignificant\
    \ experience in SQL, Python, PySpark, Scala and R\n\nProficiency in PyTorch/TensorFlow,\
    \ Spark, BigQuery\n\nExperience in creating complex data visualization tools,\
    \ frameworks and techniques.\n\nExperience in dimension reduction in big data.\n\
    \nProficient in cloud analytical stacks [ Lakes, warehouse, ETL pipelines]\n\n\
    Experience with inference platforms in AWS, Azure and other open-source platforms.\n\
    \nAre result-oriented, with a bias towards customer obsession, flexibility, and\
    \ impact.\n\nStrong written and verbal communication and teamwork skills\n\nPassion\
    \ for Large language models, NLP, and Machine Learning at scale\n\nEducation:\
    \ B.S, M.S in Computer science or Mathematics, or related field\n\nRecruitment\
    \ Process\n\nApplication Review - Phone Interview - Onsite (or Virtual Onsite)\
    \ Interview – Offer\n\nThe exact nature of the recruitment process may vary according\
    \ to the specific job and may be changed due to scheduling or other circumstances.\n\
    \nInterview schedules and the results will be informed to the applicant via the\
    \ e-mail address submitted at the application stage.\n\nDetails to Consider\n\n\
    This job posting may be closed prior to the stated end date for application if\
    \ all openings are filled.\n\nCoupang has the right to rescind an offer of employment\
    \ if a candidate is found to have submitted false information as part of the application\
    \ process.\n\nThose eligible for employment protection (recipients of veteran’\
    s benefits, the disabled, etc.) may receive preferential treatment for employment\
    \ in accordance with applicable laws.\n\nPrivacy Notice​\n\nYour personal information\
    \ will be collected and managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy\
    \ Notice located below: https://taou.cn/zlO8\n\n[Applied in Coupang.Jobs] Equal\
    \ Opportunities for All\n\nCoupang is an equal opportunity employer. Our unprecedented\
    \ success could not be possible without the valuable inputs of our globally diverse\
    \ team."
- source_job_id: "7483265"
  title: "Software Development Manager"
  description: "Description\n\n\_\n\nWe exist to wow our customers. We know we’re\
    \ doing the right thing when we hear our customers say, “How did we ever live\
    \ without Coupang?” Born out of an obsession to make shopping, eating, and living\
    \ easier than ever, we are collectively disrupting the multi-billion-dollar commerce\
    \ industry from the ground up and establishing an unparalleled reputation for\
    \ being leading and reliable force in South Korean commerce.We are proud to have\
    \ the best of both worlds — a startup culture with the resources of a large global\
    \ public company. This fuels us to continue our growth and launch new services\
    \ at the speed we have been at since our inception. We are all entrepreneurial\
    \ surrounded by opportunities to drive new initiatives and innovations. At our\
    \ core, we are bold and ambitious people that like to get our hands dirty and\
    \ make a hands-on impact. At Coupang, you will see yourself, your colleagues,\
    \ your team, and the company grow every day.Our mission to build the future of\
    \ commerce is real. We push the boundaries of what’s possible to solve problems\
    \ and break traditional tradeoffs. Join Coupang now to create an epic experience\
    \ in this always-on, high-tech, and hyper-connected world.\n\nRole Overview:\n\
    \nWe are looking for talented people who want to help shape the future of the\
    \ e-commerce markets of Korea and Asia! One of Korea’s largest innovative and\
    \ independent e-commerce firms, Coupang has revolutionised Korean customers’ shopping\
    \ experience through a constant series of innovation. With more than 12 million\
    \ customers making about 200 million purchases from Coupang, we are seeing billions\
    \ of hits every year. Coupang is engaged in a fierce competition in Korea’s e-commerce\
    \ sector, which accounts for about $60 billion of the country’s $342 billion distribution\
    \ market. Recording an average of 15-20% growth, we are on track to become a $130\
    \ billion worth firm by 2020.\n\nIn your role as the software development manager\
    \ (SDM), you will be leading a team of best-in-class engineers dedicated to projects\
    \ aimed at enhancing customer experience. Make the best use of your technical\
    \ expertise and HR management skills to create a team of smart and curious troubleshooters.\n\
    \nWhat You Will Do :\n\nAs a SDM, you will also lead the future of a system that\
    \ can fulfill computing needs based on a distributed system, high scalability,\
    \ low latency and high availability. Your other duties will include standardising\
    \ processes, tracking indices, and providing feedback regarding the system domains.\
    \ As an engineering leader, you will be expected to demonstrate technical leadership\
    \ that can help solve complicated issues and achieve a balance between strategies\
    \ and tactics.\n\nTo fulfill the role of a SDM successfully, you need to take\
    \ a customer-centered approach, delving into what delivery features they want,\
    \ and an excellent technical vision that will help attract the best engineers.\
    \ You will also be required to have the ability to motivate and guide your team\
    \ of engineers to develop their careers and grow professionally.\n\nAs the SDM,\
    \ you will:\n\nmanage an agile team of professional developers dedicated to building\
    \ a scalable, stable, and manageable system;\n\nrecruit and hire developers to\
    \ in line with the team’s goals;\n\nassist each team member with career-building\
    \ through 1:1 evaluation and counseling sessions;\n\ndefine the system architecture\
    \ with other developers;\n\nunderstand and prioritise requirements; collaborate\
    \ with product owners and stakeholders to establish a roadmap and execute plans;\n\
    \ndefine, measure, and report indices;\n\nSupport the team’s software implementation\
    \ and operation;\n\nlead improvements in development and management support;\n\
    \nlead standardisation of and improvements in business processes.\n\nBasic Qualifications:\n\
    \nmore than 10 years’ software development\n\nmore than 4 years’ software development\
    \ management and architecture-related duties\n\ngood verbal and written communication;\
    \ proven technical leadership\n\nagile software methodology\n\nPreferred Qualifications\
    \ :\n\nexcellent practical skills and expertise; implementation and operation\
    \ of large-scale, highly-scalable web service\n\nlaunching of product on time\
    \ in a dynamic environment\n\nprioritisation of tasks in an ever-changing environment\
    \ and the corresponding capabilities\n\nType of Work Model :\n\nHybrid - Coupang\
    \ hybrid work model is designed to enable a culture of collaboration that acts\
    \ a catalyst to enrich the experience of employees. Employees are required to\
    \ work at least 3 days in the office per week, with the flexibility to work from\
    \ home 2 days a week, depending on the role requirement. Some businesses may require\
    \ more time in office due to nature of work.\n\nDetails to Consider :\n\nThose\
    \ eligible for employment protection (recipients of veteran’s benefits, the disabled,\
    \ etc.) may receive preferential treatment for employment in accordance with applicable\
    \ laws.\n\nPrivacy Notice :\n\nYour personal information will be collected and\
    \ managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy Notice located below:\_\
    https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/\n\nEqual Opportunities for All :\n\n\
    Coupang is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to equal opportunity\
    \ regardless of color, ancestry, religion, sex, nation origin, sexual orientation,\
    \ age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or veteran status.\
    \ Our unprecedented success could not be possible without the valuable inputs\
    \ of our globally diverse team."
